From c15db543f4c6d509b185d6157163696514df25a8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 23:01:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(lifecycle): resolve complete process-substitution writers
 [daveey]

The output substitution opened before later operands and stdin redirects were known. Collect complete writer variants in the probe walk; apply current resolved input substitutions when feeding nested bodies. Preserve >| as a redirection, carry group feeds before suspension, and distinguish output-body stdout from input-substitution operands. Tee reads its own redirected stdin, not output operands.

Proof: 17 scan cases fail at previous reviewed head 4d8aca792b and pass now; two nested cases were additionally red on recovered WIP before current-variant expansion. Full lifecycle suite passed 1072 tests before four final cat/tee mutation controls. Combined cat-relay/group-redirections/arithmetic/feed tests passed 244. Cat/tee relay condition mutants exercised with paired positive/negative controls. Earlier base RED and 22531-command replay retained in task evidence.
